{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310458,"nonce":"KZas9JY/XVUjjqcdo98Jc5ueSLo=","title":"blinc_gpu: the data-texture primitive path is out of step with GpuPrimitive","message":"Found while adding fields to GpuPrimitive. Read from source; the path was not run (it is the no-storage-buffer fallback, WebGL2).\n\nThe renderer sizes the primitive data texture at 23 texels (width: 23, bytes_per_row: 23 * 16, \"Each GpuPrimitive is 23 x vec4\u003cf32\u003e\") and the _dt shaders load 23 fields by texel index. GpuPrimitive has 24 vec4 fields before the per-side colours and 28 after. clip_corner_shape was inserted into the struct at field 10 and never into the loader:\n\n- load_primitive in sdf_core_dt.wgsl reads gradient_params at texel 10, rotation at 11, and so on, one behind the struct from field 10 on, and never loads clip_corner_shape. calculate_clip_alpha reads that field, so it is zero there.\n- The upload copies GpuPrimitive bytes with a row stride of 23 * 16 against a 24 * 16 struct, so every row after the first starts mid-primitive.\n\nThe same holds for the other _dt shaders. tests/primitive_layout.rs guards the struct declarations in all twelve shaders but not these loaders or the texture width, which is how it went unseen.\n\nThe _vb and _dt core shaders are also hand-kept forks, not copies. Their border compositing is the older four-component mix that sdf_core replaced with a source-over composite, so a fix to sdf_core did not reach them.\n\nFix: load every field in struct order in each _dt shader, size the texture and the upload from the struct's size, and extend primitive_layout.rs to parse load_primitive and compare it with the struct, as it does the declarations. Then decide whether the _vb and _dt forks should be generated from the base shader the way the prelude is.\n\nRelated: fa2406c (blinc_gpu catches up with the blinc_abi display list), which adds fields and so widens this gap.","files":null}]}